On 24 Aug., 01:16, ran...@pactechdata.com wrote:
> On Aug 23, 2:58 pm, eXcel <red.sec...@gmx.net> wrote:
>
> > I just had an unfortunate accident with a gremlin. It hit me and then
> > chuckled, meaning it took some intrinsic, right? However, I didn't get
> > any clue about *which* intrinsic it stole. It just chuckled.
> [...]
> > If not, what else could he have taken, i.e. which intrinsic generally
> > doesn't provide a message when you lose it?
>
>      There is always a message if an _intrinsic_ is taken,
> but there is no message--after the chuckling--when it randomly
> chooses an attribute for which you lack the intrinsic.  One of
> the candidates is aggrevate monster, so you wouldn't have seen
> any message if you didn't have that as an intrinsic.
>
>      Losing protection from that attack always gives the "you
> feel vulnerable" message.  Disintegration resistance is not a
> candidate for that intrinsic-loss effect.  (But if it was,
> wearing something which duplicated it would not have suppressed
> the corresponding you-feel-whatever message.)

